  "style": {
    "01_script": "Traditional Chinese, Taiwan standard character forms (教育部標準字): 為 裡 眾 群 峰 說 溫 吳 黃 戶 稅 內 線 著 啟 衛 綠 鑑 橫 劍 槍 糧 遊; never Simplified or HK/old variants (爲 裏 衆 羣 峯 説 温 吴 粮 衞). Mind one-to-many traps: 徵兵 but 出征; 鐘 (bell) vs surname 鍾; surnames 范 岳 沈 葉 單 stay as in the names table.",
    "02_punctuation": "Full-width CJK punctuation: ，。、；：！？（）「」 (nested 『』), ……; no spaces between CJK text, placeholders and numbers (兵力{troops}, 金{gold}, 第{day}日). Keep ASCII format symbols that carry layout or numbers: '/', '%', '+', '-', 'x', '~', '^', 'v', '.' in compact formats ({value} / {max}, {year}.{month}, 1x, ~{value}, {column} ^) stay as in English. UI labels and buttons have no final 。; full sentences end with 。 or ！.",
    "03_register": "Koei Taiwan register: concise semi-literary modern Chinese with light classical flavour (我軍、敵軍、主公、陣亡、潰散); no internet slang, no heavy 文言. Advisors and subjects address the player as 主公 (Azure Court: 殿下; Wolf Riders: 大汗; Southern Lotus: 主上; Black Mountain: 大哥). System messages avoid 你/您 where possible and use 我方 / 我軍 for the player's side (Your turn → 我方回合, your cities → 我方城市).",
    "04_placeholders": "Keep every {placeholder} exactly; reorder freely for Chinese word order. No plural forms: add measure words after numeric placeholders: 座 (cities: {count}座城), 名 (officers, soldiers, prisoners), 支 (armies, units), 個 (factions), 個月 (months), 日 (days). Amount patterns: '{n} gold' → 金{n}, '{n} food' → 兵糧{n}, '{n} troops' → 兵力{n} (narrative may use {n}名士兵 / 率兵{n}); casualties '{damage} casualties ({troops} left)' → 損兵{damage}（剩餘{troops}）. Do not add 軍 directly after {faction} (鐵旗軍軍): use {faction}部隊 / {faction}的軍團.",
    "05_articles_possessives": "Drop English articles before names (the {faction} → {faction}). Possessive {unit}'s → {unit}的 or {unit}部隊. Gender of placeholder officers is unknown: avoid 他/她 for {officer}/{target}/{unit}; repeat the placeholder, use 其, or omit the subject. Fixed scenario characters may use 他/她 per the English.",
    "06_names": "Use the names section verbatim (Traditional forms of nameZh). Chinese names take no spaces or middle dots; compound surnames (慕容 赫連 拓跋 獨孤 上官 歐陽 司徒 東方 南宮) stay whole. Epithet display '{name}, {epithet}' → 「{epithet}」{name}; in prose quote an epithet as 人稱「快刀」. Faction prose short forms: the Iron Banner 鐵旗軍, the League 東海盟, the Brotherhood 黑山寨, the Azure Court / the court (in Azure context) 青庭 / 朝廷. Sect short forms: Cloudpeak 雲峰劍派, Stone Bell 石鐘寺, Moonwell 月井堂. Yanmen Pass as the city label is 雁門 (from nameZh); prose about the mountain pass itself may say 雁門關; Jade Gate = 玉門關 (the pass at 玉門).",
    "07_quotes": "Technique names, event titles and chosen options inside sentences go in 「」: 習得絕技「{technique}」, 「{title}」：選擇了「{choice}」. Labels and lists do not quote them. English straight quotes and apostrophes become 「」 / 『』.",
    "08_ui_length": "UI (ui.*): buttons, tabs and labels ideally <= 8 characters; tabs 2 characters (內政 軍事 外交 人事 市井); stat names and short stat names 2 characters (武力 統率 智力 政治 魅力); order buttons use Koei 2-character names (開墾 商業 巡察 城防 徵兵 訓練 搜索 登用 移動 輸送 褒賞 贈禮 出征). Ellipsis on buttons: one '…' (登用…); in prose '……'. Short status flashes end with ！ (潰散！ 陣亡！).",
    "09_dates_numbers": "Dates: Year {year}, Month {month}, Day {day} → {year}年{month}月{day}日; seasons are single characters 春 夏 秋 冬 shown in （） or after ・ ({season}・規劃). Battle days 第{day}日; 'Day {day} of {days}' → 第{day}日（共{days}日）. Keep Arabic numerals (do not write 三百 for 300 in UI/log text); in narrative prose with no placeholder, Chinese numerals are fine (二百步, 三萬大軍).",
    "10_allusions": "Keep the Three Kingdoms / wuxia allusions recognisable: Three Visits → 三顧 (三顧茅廬); the Sleeping Crane 臥鶴 (echo of 臥龍); the Prince's Amnesty → 招安 (水滸); General Who Pacifies the South → 平南將軍; Mandate of Heaven → 天命; the Grey Wolf → 蒼狼; the summit tournament at Cloudpeak → 峰頂論劍.",
    "11_sentences": "Instructions/errors are polite and short: 'Choose X.' → 請選擇X。; 'Not enough gold: {cost} needed, {gold} in {city}.' → 金錢不足：需要{cost}，{city}僅有{gold}。; 'X can only be done during the planning phase.' → 只能在規劃階段X。 Rumors open with 聽說 / 據說; log lines are past-tense reports without pronouns."
  },
